ELF Practical – From Object File to Running Process


Introduction

This project demonstrates ELF (Executable and Linkable Format) in Ubuntu Linux.

Practical Topics

1. Creating a C program
2. Compiling source code into an object file
3. Exploring ELF headers
4. Exploring ELF sections
5. Symbol table
6. Relocation information
7. Disassembly using objdump
8. Creating an executable file
9. Program headers and segments
10. Dynamic linking
11. ELF32 and ELF64
12. Running a program in Linux

Commands and Tools

- GCC
- readelf
- objdump
- file
- ldd
- Linux Terminal

